{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":23,"at":"2026-10-31T14:28:24.704Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C003-CH1-R0365","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Proposed go/no-go: at least two of three confirmation specimens match field crack location and morphology, with repeatable factor contrasts exceeding measurement uncertainty.","sources":[{"recordId":"C003-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"A good outcome would be understanding exactly what is causing the cracks so we can change our welding procedure, filler material, or joint design and stop the warranty replacements.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"},{"recordId":"C003-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"We have photos and measurements of the cracked joints from site visits, and we still have two of the failed sections in storage.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"The two-of-three count does not define what qualifies as a field match, and contrasts exceeding instrument uncertainty can still reflect specimen scatter, permitting false acceptance of meaningful failure reproduction. Add a compact prerequisite freezing a field-location/morphology scoring rubric and uncertain-reference handling before confirmation, plus a specified sampling-aware confidence-bound or equivalent acceptance rule for the factor contrasts; unresolved reference classifications or insufficient precision should remain inconclusive.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":24,"at":"2026-10-31T14:28:29.979Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-review-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1},"kind":"review","inputs":[{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-review-C001-CH1-R1008.v1.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":25,"at":"2026-10-31T14:28:29.979Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Select the best configuration on tuning data, then evaluate Modbus and BACnet separately using held-out client traffic and isolated-bench injections, including persistent anomalies and process changes.","sources":[],"explanation":"“Best” has no selection criterion, so the design does not establish how configurations will be chosen without attack labels or how the selection will remain separate from held-out results. Add a brief prerequisite to freeze a label-free tuning objective, constraints and tie-break rule before held-out evaluation.","owner":"proposal_writer"},{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Proposed go/no-go targets are at least 80% of injected episodes detected within 60 seconds, a 95% upper confidence bound no greater than one false episode per observed site-day, and at least 80% correct plant-manager interpretation tasks.","sources":[],"explanation":"Recall and comprehension can pass on small or favourable samples without a stated statistical acceptance rule; recall also lacks an injection-to-alert matching rule, and comprehension could pass trivial tasks without testing useful alert understanding. Make acceptance conditional on predefining injection matching and timing, representative interpretation tasks with a correctness rubric and denominator, and confidence-bound or equivalent evidence rules for both 80% targets separately by protocol.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":26,"at":"2026-10-31T14:28:32.905Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},"kind":"proposal","inputs":[{"artifactId":"business-C009-CH1","version":1},{"artifactId":"scholar-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},{"artifactId":"pair-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-C009-CH1-R0288.v1.json"}}
