{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":29,"at":"2026-10-31T14:29:04.636Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-review-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},"kind":"review","inputs":[{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-review-C009-CH1-R0288.v1.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":30,"at":"2026-10-31T14:29:04.636Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Report telecom, mixed-script and unseen-term results separately.","sources":[{"recordId":"C009-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"We need an approach that handles lemmatisation or indexing in a way that is accurate for Serbian, tolerates script mixing automatically, and can be updated when new vocabulary arrives without a full re-index.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"},{"recordId":"C009","field":"about","quote":"today we serve four banks and two telecoms providers across Serbia","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"The bank-wide confidence bound could pass while mixed-script queries, new terminology or telecom queries remain unacceptable, because separate reporting does not constrain acceptance. Add a prerequisite to agree separate acceptance criteria and sufficient evaluation evidence for these populations; the company need not adopt the bank's numerical threshold for every subset.","owner":"proposal_writer"},{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Proposed go/no-go: the selected configuration's upper 95% confidence bound is below 5% on a separate held-out sample from the original bank population, with no precision loss against baseline.","sources":[],"explanation":"The miss-rate gate is defined, but the additional precision gate has no retrieval cutoff, counted unit, aggregation rule or statistical acceptance condition, so different reasonable measurements could produce opposite decisions. Briefly make agreement on a precision definition and paired uncertainty-based no-loss rule a prerequisite to tuning and evaluation.","owner":"proposal_writer"},{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Go/no-go additionally requires sustained below-5% bank performance, an agreed maintenance-hours ceiling, tooling/data costs within approximately EUR 8,000, and a testable prototype within six months.","sources":[{"recordId":"C009-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"A good outcome is getting that 18% miss rate below 5% and keeping it there with a manageable maintenance process.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"“Sustained” has no defined update sequence, evaluation exposure or statistical rule, allowing a single favorable post-update replay to stand in for keeping the miss rate below 5% as vocabulary changes. Require an agreed sequence of vocabulary-update rounds with independent post-update evaluation and an explicit confidence-based acceptance rule, which can be stated as a prerequisite within the existing length.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":31,"at":"2026-10-31T14:29:21.355Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-review-C003-CH1-R0365","version":2},"kind":"review","inputs":[{"artifactId":"proposal-C003-CH1-R0365","version":2}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-review-C003-CH1-R0365.v2.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":32,"at":"2026-10-31T14:29:21.355Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C003-CH1-R0365","version":2},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Repeatable factor contrasts must have simultaneous 95% confidence intervals accounting for specimen and batch scatter wholly beyond measurement uncertainty, with consistent confirmation direction.","sources":[],"explanation":"The gate does not identify which measured response and exposure basis these contrasts concern or connect them to field-matching failures: a configuration could match the field fractures while an unrelated contrast in strain or crack life supplies statistical significance, without explaining the service failure. Add a prerequisite to freeze the primary response, exposure/stopping rule and explanatory contrasts before confirmation, and require acceptance to link those contrasts to field-matching damage, allowing room-temperature reproduction as an alternative finding.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":33,"at":"2026-10-31T14:29:22.132Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-review-C001-CH1-R1008","version":2},"kind":"review","inputs":[{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":2}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-review-C001-CH1-R1008.v2.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":34,"at":"2026-10-31T14:29:22.133Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":2},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"95% upper confidence bound at most one false episode per observed site-day","sources":[{"recordId":"C001-CH1","field":"text","quote":"We need to detect unusual behaviour on Modbus and BACnet networks without labelled attack data — our clients have never been breached (or don't know it), so we have zero examples of malicious traffic and supervised classifiers are useless to us.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"},{"recordId":"C001-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"it flagged so many false positives in real deployments that clients started switching the alerts off.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"Unlike recall and comprehension, the false-alert gate is not explicitly required separately for Modbus and BACnet, so pooling episodes and site-days could pass while one protocol remains unusably noisy. Require the stated upper confidence bound separately for each protocol, using fully monitored site-days with that protocol present as its exposure denominator.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-27-00-166Z","seq":35,"at":"2026-10-31T14:29:26.163Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":2},"kind":"proposal","inputs":[{"artifactId":"business-C009-CH1","version":1},{"artifactId":"scholar-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},{"artifactId":"pair-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-C009-CH1-R0288.v2.json"}}
